# shell: desktop
# home: fixture
# prefs: factory
# setup: benchstop
# board: only
# Stopping a bench run, and the board afterwards.
#
# A run holds the board's port for as long as it lasts, so stopping one
# has to give the board back -- otherwise a run somebody changed their
# mind about costs the shell its board until the run would have ended
# anyway.  That is what is checked here: stopped EARLY, and the board is
# the shell's again well before the run could have finished.
wait 60
click 980 30
wait 10
menu-pick Applications
wait 10
menu-pick Bench
wait 250
expect-title Bench
click-window Bench
wait 8
key Down
wait 3
key Down
wait 3
key Down
wait 3
key Down
wait 3
key Down
wait 3
key Down
wait 3
key Down
wait 3
key Down
wait 3
wait 8
click 71 8
wait 8
expect-menu Show the parts of link-console
menu-pick Run on tiku
note far enough in to be a run, nowhere near far enough to be over
wait 150
click-window Bench
wait 8
click 71 8
wait 8
note the board is away because THIS application asked for it, so the
note list does not reshuffle under the row somebody chose
expect-menu Show the parts of link-console
expect-menu Stop
menu-pick Stop
note and the board is back at once -- the whole of this run would still
note have been going
wait 250
expect-read /devices/tiku/sys/device/name tiku
quit
